    "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Centre-for-Remote-Health-Alice-Springs/Casual-Professional-Academic-Register---Rural-and-Remote-Health-NT_JR0000011671-1": {
      "title": "Casual Professional/Academic Register – Rural and Remote Health NT",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-02-26\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAbout Flinders Our bold ambition, articulated in our Strategic Plan Impact. With Purpose: The 2035 Agenda , is to change 10 million lives for the better by opening opportunities, solving real‑world problems, and translating knowledge into outcomes that strengthen communities.   With a renewed focus on putting students first, being the university for industry and enterprise, and delivering research that creates meaningful impact, we recognise that exceptional people are central to our success. Casual Register Flinders Rural and Remote Health NT At   Flinders Rural and Remote Health NT , our aim is to be a hub for innovative health research, education, and workforce development across the Northern Territory.  We engage with students, community, and stakeholders to provide critical programs, such as the Northern Territory Medical Program, Paramedicine, Rural Clinical School, and the University Department of Rural Health. Our postgraduate education pathways (Remote Health Practice program), provides workforce development through Indigenous health and clinical skills training, and we have a community driven research program led by researchers committed to improving health outcomes. We work alongside Poche SA+NT focussing on Indigenous leadership capacity development and developing the Indigenous health workforce.  All activities are driven by our values which focus on the long-term and short-term needs of the NT community. Casual Register Flinders University has a number of Casual Registers as a means of expressions of interest for the purpose of casual work, should such opportunities arise. This casual register applies specifically to our Rural and Remote Health NT Campuses. These campuses include: Alice Springs Darwin Katherine Nhulunbuy Tennant Creek How to Register: Upload your current CV/Resume detailing your qualifications and experience You may choose to upload a Cover Letter of no more than 1 page to support your CV/Resume Your application will be acknowledged by an automated e-mail once submitted. If a casual opportunity is available and your application is considered suitable, the relevant hiring manager will contact you for a further discussion. Please note, only suitable applicants will be contacted. Applying to the Casual Register does not guarantee employment. Further Information: Northern Territory Government legislation (the Care and Protection of Children Act 2007) now requires all individuals in child related employment or whose duties involve, or are likely to involve, contact with a child, to hold a valid ‘Working with Children Clearance’ (Ochre Card). This position involves child related work and is assessed as requiring a Working with Children Clearance/Ochre Card Please contact Recruitment@Flinders by email at recruitment@flinders.edu.au  should you have any queries regarding Casual opportunities."
    },
    "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Casual-Professional-Register--Flinders-Students_JR0000012092": {
      "title": "Casual Professional Register - Flinders Students",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-02-26\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAbout Flinders Our bold ambition, articulated in our Strategic Plan Impact. With Purpose: The 2035 Agenda , is to change 10 million lives for the better by opening opportunities, solving real‑world problems, and translating knowledge into outcomes that strengthen communities.   With a renewed focus on putting students first, being the university for industry and enterprise, and delivering research that creates meaningful impact, we recognise that exceptional people are central to our success. Casual Register Flinders University has a range of casual job opportunities available for current students across its various campuses, including: Bedford Park Flinders City Campus Tonsley Flinders in the Northern Territory Flinders University operates year-round and requires casual employees to support events, projects, and the general day-to-day operations of the University. We value our students and are committed to offering opportunities that help them develop their skills, expand their capabilities, and foster meaningful relationships. If this opportunity interests you, we strongly encourage you to apply to our casual professional register. Please note, only students currently enrolled at the Flinders University are eligible to apply for this register. How does the Casual register work? Flinders University has a number of Casual Registers as a means of expressions of interest for the purpose of casual work, should such opportunities arise. We recognise the key to our success is exceptional people and we welcome registrations of interest from current Flinders students wishing to join our team on a casual or short-term basis. If a casual opportunity is available and your application is considered suitable, the relevant hiring manager will contact you for a further discussion. Applying to the Casual Register does not guarantee employment. How to Apply and Information: Upload your current CV detailing your qualifications and experience. You may choose to upload a Cover Letter of no more than 1 page to support your CV/Resumé. Please contact Recruitment@Flinders by email at recruitment@flinders.edu.au  should you have any queries regarding casual opportunities. Prescribed Conditions for Employment (If Applicable): You may be required to provide a valid Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check which is satisfactory to the University. You may be required to provide a current Working With Children Check which is satisfactory to the University in accordance with the Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (SA)."
    },
